---
import Tool from '../../layouts/Tool.astro';
---
<Tool title="Dimensional weight checker" description="Check whether a parcel is billed on actual or dimensional weight, using the dimensional divisor from your own carrier rate guide, and see how much box volume to cut." lede="Carriers can bill on the greater of actual and dimensional weight. Enter your carrier's divisor for the service you use and see which one governs.">
  <form slot="calc" class="calc" id="dw" onsubmit="return false">
    <div class="calc-in"><h2>Your parcel</h2>
      <div class="field"><label for="u">Units</label><select id="u"><option value="in">Inches &amp; pounds</option><option value="cm">Centimeters &amp; kilograms</option></select></div>
      <div class="field-row"><div class="field"><label for="l">Length</label><input id="l" type="number" min="0" step="0.1" value="14" /></div><div class="field"><label for="w">Width</label><input id="w" type="number" min="0" step="0.1" value="10" /></div></div>
      <div class="field-row"><div class="field"><label for="h">Height</label><input id="h" type="number" min="0" step="0.1" value="6" /></div><div class="field"><label for="a">Actual weight</label><input id="a" type="number" min="0" step="0.01" value="3" /></div></div>
      <div class="field"><label for="d">Dimensional divisor <span class="hint">Required. Copy it from your carrier's current rate guide or contract — it differs by carrier, service and agreement.</span></label><input id="d" type="number" min="1" step="1" placeholder="From your rate guide" /></div>
      <button class="btn btn-cta" type="submit">Check</button>
    </div>
    <div class="calc-out" aria-live="polite"><h2>Billable weight</h2>
      <div class="out big"><span>Greater of the two</span><span class="v" id="o-b">—</span></div>
      <div class="out"><span>Dimensional weight</span><span class="v" id="o-d">—</span></div>
      <div class="out"><span>Actual weight</span><span class="v" id="o-a">—</span></div>
      <div class="out"><span>Rounded up</span><span class="v" id="o-r">—</span></div>
      <p class="verdict" id="o-v">Enter your carrier's divisor to see the result.</p>
    </div>
  </form>
  <h2>The formula</h2>
  <p>Dimensional weight = length × width × height ÷ divisor. With inches the result is in pounds; with centimeters, kilograms. Billable weight is the greater of dimensional and actual weight, often rounded up to the next whole unit. Measure the packed parcel at its widest points, and check how your carrier rounds each side before multiplying.</p>
  <h2>Why there is no default divisor</h2>
  <p>Divisors vary by carrier, by service and by negotiated contract, and carriers change them. A single default would be wrong for many readers, so the field stays empty until you copy the figure from your own rate guide.</p>
  <h2>Worked example (hypothetical divisor)</h2>
  <p>A packed box measures 14 × 10 × 8 inches and weighs 4 pounds on the scale. Its volume is 1,120 cubic inches. With a divisor of 139 (an example only; use your carrier's figure), the dimensional weight is 1,120 ÷ 139 ≈ 8.06 pounds. That is more than the 4-pound actual weight, so the box is billed on its size. To let actual weight govern at that divisor, the box would need to shrink to about 556 cubic inches (4 × 139) — for example 12 × 9 × 5 inches, which is 540.</p>
  <h2>Ways to lower billed weight</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Measure the packed parcel, not the product: bulges, handles and void fill all count.</li>
    <li>Test a smaller carton size or a mailer for light items; a few inches on each side compounds because the three sides multiply.</li>
    <li>Compare the result under each service you use: divisors and rounding rules can differ between ground and express services of the same carrier.</li>
    <li>For many small units, check whether one master carton bills lower than several separate parcels.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Where to find your divisor</h2>
  <p>Carriers publish their divisors and measuring rules in their service guides or rate documents, and negotiated contracts can change them. Copy the figure that applies to your account and service, and note the date you checked it, because divisors are revised. Marketplace fulfillment programs set their own size tiers and dimensional rules; for those, use the program's fee page rather than a carrier divisor.</p>
  <script>
    const $ = (id: string) => document.getElementById(id) as HTMLInputElement;
    function run() {
      const cm = $('u').value === 'cm', L = +$('l').value, W = +$('w').value, H = +$('h').value, A = +$('a').value, D = +$('d').value, u = cm ? 'kg' : 'lb', vu = cm ? 'cm³' : 'in³', vol = L * W * H;
      $('o-a').textContent = `${A} ${u}`;
      if (!(D > 0)) { ['o-b', 'o-d', 'o-r'].forEach((i) => ($(i).textContent = '—')); $('o-v').textContent = "Enter your carrier's divisor to see the result."; return; }
      const dim = vol / D, b = Math.max(dim, A);
      $('o-d').textContent = `${dim.toFixed(2)} ${u}`; $('o-b').textContent = `${b.toFixed(2)} ${u}`; $('o-r').textContent = `${Math.ceil(b - 1e-9)} ${u}`;
      $('o-v').textContent = dim > A ? `Box size drives the bill. Cutting volume by ${(vol - A * D).toLocaleString('en-US', { maximumFractionDigits: 0 })} ${vu} would let actual weight govern.` : 'Actual weight governs; a smaller box would not lower the billed weight.';
    }
    document.getElementById('dw')!.addEventListener('input', run); document.getElementById('dw')!.addEventListener('submit', run); run();
  </script>
</Tool>
